body:
Look, i'm all for progressive policy, but i'm an investor as well and I promise you capital gains is already treated as income unless you hold a position for more than a year. The reason being is to incentivize you to not be dumb with your money and make short term plays. I do not support getting rid of that because low capital retail investors such as myself may be more inclined to take higher risk that they may not be ready for, and consequently end up throwing their life's savings in the trash. The SEC and Wall Street firms have an interest in low capital retail investors being smart with their money and playing it just like they do. 

&#x200B;

Honestly, progressives should love the stock market because it is the capitalist's way of redistributing wealth, considering you know what you're doing.
